SDL video backend: Cedar hardware H.264/HEVC decode (tg5040)

Adds a hardware decode path for the Allwinner A133P (TrimUI Brick Pro) to the
SDL video backend, opt-in at run time with MOONLIGHT_HWDEC=1. Unset, or any
other value, keeps the FFmpeg decoder, so the pak behaves as before until the
launcher exports the variable.

The decoder is the device's CedarC v1.3.0 library, driven through dlopen()
(src/cedar/), so nothing new is linked and the engine still starts on a
firmware without the vendor libraries: sdl_setup() then logs why and uses
FFmpeg. Decoded NV21 pictures are converted to the YV12 texture input in CPU
and delivered through the same SDL_USEREVENT the FFmpeg path pushes, so the
existing present path and the wrapper's framebuffer contract are unchanged.
The renderer callbacks keep CAPABILITY_DIRECT_SUBMIT, as with FFmpeg.

decode loop, pending-picture accounting, PPS/AUD frame closing, stall rebuild
and DR_NEED_IDR handling are ported from isalin/moonlight-tsp
(GPL-3.0-or-later) src/video_cedar.c; tsp's disp2/G2D/ION display half is not
ported. Sources of truth and the spike that proved the ABI on the device:
engine/cedar-hwdec/. This patch is regenerated from them by
engine/cedar-hwdec/scripts/make-engine-patch.sh.

Applies after sdl-buffer-1.patch and latency-debug.patch on
moonlight-embedded 274d3db34da764344a7a402ee74e6080350ac0cd.

